## Deliverable paths
- **`/app/agent-output/H5/report.md`** — primary report (also mirrored to `/app/agent-output/H5/README.md`, `/app/agent-output/H5/migration-report.md`, `/app/agent-output/report.md`, `/app/agent-output/migration-report.md` since the statement names only the `/app/agent-output/` directory)
- **`/app/agent-output/H5/evidence/`** — raw evidence: git diff of the fixture, install/build/test logs, `pnpm pack` manifest + sha256, isolated-profile manifest, `--dump-config`, migrated/baseline cold-boot outputs, direct-import/link-masking proof, activation-check output

## What the report establishes (from pipeline evidence + my own re-verification)
- **Root cause**: `src/index.ts` still imported the runtime helper `settingsNamespace()` from `@deepseek-ai/dsh-settings`; alpha.2 removed it (runtime exports now only `SettingsConflictError` / `SettingsProvider` / `default` / `redactSecrets`), so the ESM named import fails at instantiation and Cordis fails the whole tree. The plugin-local 0.1.1-rc.2 `node_modules` masked this on link installs.
- **Migration, by card**: **DSH-0.1.2-A2-10** (literal namespace straight into `ctx.settings.register()` under compile-time `SettingsNamespaceInput`; test double uses `as SettingsNamespace`) and **DSH-0.1.2-A2-03** (cohort alignment: `dsh-settings`/`dsh-brand` 0.1.2-alpha.2, `cordis` 4.0.2, `schemastery` 3.18.2, lockfile regenerated, zero `0.1.1-rc.2` residue). All 36 cards are ledgered (2 done / 34 not-needed with reasons).
- **Independent verification**: clean offline `pnpm install --frozen-lockfile` (21 pkgs, 0 downloads, exact versions) → typecheck/build/test 1/1 + `--skipLibCheck false` diagnostic green → `pnpm pack` (no node_modules in tarball) → fresh isolated `DSH_HOME` profile with bundles `@deepseek-ai/dsh-base` + `@deepseek-ai/dsh-headless` + plugin → cold boot reaches the application layer (`TRANSPORT … 127.0.0.1:9`), no pending, no plugin tree failed; direct `settings.describe()` returns `h5-runtime-drift` / `{greeting:'hello from h5'}` / `applies:'live'`. The preserved baseline tarball reproduces the failure and link-masking on the same host.
- **Caveats recorded**: `/app/fixture`'s untracked `node_modules/` is still the stale 0.1.1-rc.2 tree (in-place `tsc` fails TS2345; a clean install is required — this is the masking condition itself); sibling peers resolve to 0.1.2-rc.1 via caret; no host peer enforcement at alpha.2; no client half / live-reload / non-Linux coverage.

`/app/fixture` was not modified by me — `git status` shows only the pre-existing pipeline changes plus the new `/app/agent-output/`.

